# Fast, SHORT-CONTEXT profile. Tested 2026-10-13: RTX 5060 8GB (desktop session), i7-12700F,
# 32GB RAM, llama.cpp b11576. UD-IQ1_M with the whole model on the GPU via CUDA managed memory.
#
# Result with prompts up to ~4K tokens: ~32 tok/s writing new code, ~110 tok/s rewriting
# existing code (ngram speculation, ~99% acceptance), ~600 tok/s prompt processing.
#
# Limits, measured, not guessed:
#  - Managed memory oversubscribes VRAM. Past ~5K tokens of context the KV pages evict
#    weights and generation collapses to ~0.4-5 tok/s. QLC_CTX is therefore capped at 4096.
#    This profile is NOT suitable for coding agents (their system prompts alone exceed 4K).
#  - 1.75-bit weights: HumanEval-20 15/20 (quality profile 19/20); thinking does not recover it.
#  - The first request after start is slow (~5 tok/s) while pages migrate.
QLC_MODEL=UD-IQ1_M
QLC_UNIFIED_MEMORY=1
QLC_CTX=4096
QLC_CPU_FFN=0
QLC_THREADS=6
QLC_UBATCH=512
QLC_KV_TYPE=q8_0
QLC_SPEC_TYPE=ngram-mod
QLC_MIN_FREE_VRAM_MIB=6600
